In article <1990Feb20.002953.5234@ux1.cso.uiuc.edu> murphy@symcom.symcom.math.uiuc.edu (Michael L. Murphy) writes:
>
>    Hello there.  Here's a question to the makers of Nethack (or anyone
>else that can answer it, actually.)
>    I usually dialup my local UNIX box using a terminal emulator on my IBM
>that I know is perfectly capable of 16-color graphics and lettering.  I
>am able to set it to VT100, ANSI, and a host of other term types.  I
>compiled Nethack V3.0.6 here with COLOR defined.  I have set color in
>my NETHACKOPTIONS environment variable.  I have tried both set term ANSI
>and set term VT100.  My question (if it isn't already obvious):  Why
>won't the monsters appear in different colors, like in PC Nethack?  Do I
>have to modify the /etc/termcap file?  Do I have to modify the (shudder)
>NetHack source itself?  Oh, wisest of NetHack gods, guide me along the
>correct course, so that I may never mistake my pet for a jackal again.
>

Try this:
Make sure that both color and standout are set as options.

Set TERM to kermitpc  (i.e. put a "setenv TERM kermitpc" in your
.cshrc).

Set TERMCAP to ~/kermitcap  (i.e. put a "setenv TERMCAP ~/kermitpc"
in your .cshrc).

Cut out the following termcap, and stick it in a file in your home
directory and call it "kermitcap"

--------------- cut here -------------------

